;
; SkoolKit ref file for the Currah μSpeech
;
; To build the HTML disassembly, run these commands:
;   sna2skool.py -H -o 0 -c sources/microspeech.ctl CURRAH.ROM > sources/microspeech.skool
;   utils/mkhtml.py

[Config]
Expand=#INCLUDE(Expand)
RefFiles=bases.ref;analytics.ref;changelog.ref;facts.ref;sound.ref
GameDir=microspeech

[Game]
Game=Currah μSpeech
Copyright=&copy; 1983 Currah &copy; 2024 ArcadeGeek LTD.
Repository=https://github.com/pobtastic/currah/
LinkInternalOperands=1
AddressAnchor={address#IF({base}==16)(:04x)}

[PageHeaders]
GameIndex=The complete<>ROM disassembly (work in progress)
TryIt=Try s$
Sound=Allophones

[Index:Reference:Reference]
Facts
TryIt
Sound
Credits
Changelog

[Paths]
Changelog=reference/changelog.html
Credits=reference/credits.html
TryIt=reference/tryit.html
Sound=sound/sounds.html

[Titles+]
TryIt=Try s$
Sound=Allophones

[Resources]
uspeech.css=.
audio/*.wav={AudioPath}

[Page:TryIt]
JavaScript=allophones.js;uspeech.js
PageContent=#INCLUDE(TryIt)

[TryIt]
<link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="../uspeech.css" />
<div class="uspeech">
  <p>Type a Currah speech string as you would assign to
  #FACT(sstring,s$) and hear the #FACT(sp0256,SP0256-AL2)
  allophones that #R$021F would queue. This is not English
  text-to-speech: letters map one-for-one, and names in
  parentheses pick a specific sound.</p>
  <label for="uspeech-input">s$=</label>
  <textarea id="uspeech-input" spellcheck="false"
    aria-describedby="uspeech-status">he(ll)(oo)</textarea>
  <div class="uspeech-row">
    <button type="button" id="uspeech-speak">Speak</button>
    <button type="button" id="uspeech-stop">Stop</button>
    <span class="uspeech-note">Ctrl+Enter also speaks.</span>
  </div>
  <p>Examples from the 1983 manual:</p>
  <div class="uspeech-row uspeech-examples">
    <button type="button" data-uspeech="he(ll)(oo)">he(ll)(oo)</button>
    <button type="button" data-uspeech="kw(ee)n">kw(ee)n</button>
    <button type="button" data-uspeech="boks">boks</button>
    <button type="button" data-uspeech="sp(EE)k n(oo) (EE)vil">sp(EE)k n(oo) (EE)vil</button>
    <button type="button" data-uspeech="a(tt)">a(tt)</button>
    <button type="button" data-uspeech="(dth)en">(dth)en</button>
    <button type="button" data-uspeech="s(er)cul">s(er)cul</button>
  </div>
  <p id="uspeech-status" class="uspeech-status" role="status"></p>
  <p id="uspeech-marked" class="uspeech-marked" hidden></p>
  <p>Queued allophones (bit 6 set means high intonation). Click
  one to hear it alone:</p>
  <div id="uspeech-tokens" class="uspeech-tokens"></div>
  <p>A full stop queues a sentence pause. A space is a word
  pause, a comma is a phrase pause, and an apostrophe is a
  short pause. Uppercase raises the pitch. Q and X are not
  letters in this alphabet; write "kw" and "ks" instead.</p>
  <p>The parser follows #R$021F and #R$02EB. Samples are
  recordings of a real AL2 chip, concatenated in the browser;
  they are close to the unit, not a cycle-accurate
  #FACT(sp0256,SP0256) core.</p>
</div>

